WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:03.291
[Rogue] <i>Previously on</i> X-Men...

2
00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:06.624
[Nightcrawler] <i>I was abandoned
by my mother. Mystique. as an infant.</i>

3
00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:10.707
<i>Despite our shared blood.
I was too blue for her.</i>

4
00:00:10.708 --> 00:00:13.541
<i>Then. I met Rogue years later.</i>

5
00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:16.374
<i>We could have been enemies or strangers.</i>

6
00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:18.707
<i>Instead. unlike our mother.</i>

7
00:00:18.708 --> 00:00:21.332
<i>we chose not to abandon each other.</i>

8
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:24.666
[Beast] <i>Perhaps the Professor's vision
for the future was too near-sighted</i>

9
00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:28.042
and begging for tolerance
was our first mistake.

10
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.791
When Logan told me Graydon Creed
was your kid. I couldn't see it.

11
00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:33.541
but now... [shivers]

12
00:00:33.542 --> 00:00:34.666
can't unsee it.

13
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.874
Shoulda killed the little mistake
when I had the chance.

14
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:40.457
[Professor X] <i>My X-Men must now evolve.</i>

15
00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:44.541
<i>Ladies and gentlemen. I give you X-Corp.</i>

16
00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:48.374
If Charles Xavier thinks
that he can skirt federal laws

17
00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:51.249
by re-establishing his X-Men overseas.

18
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.625
he should be prepared for the blowback.

19
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.833
[opening theme music playing]

20
00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:15.125
[people screaming]

21
00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:35.000
Sister. what madness is this?

22
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:41.167
[gasps]

23
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.583
[grunts]

24
00:02:50.292 --> 00:02:51.917
- You're safe now.
- [male mutant] Thank you.

25
00:03:00.958 --> 00:03:02.083
Illyana.

26
00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:04.583
Illyana.

27
00:03:14.917 --> 00:03:16.333
Illyana!

28
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:20.375
No!

29
00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:28.708
Illyana!

30
00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:34.832
[male announcer] <i>Ladies and gentlemen.
Friends of Humanity.</i>

31
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:38.458
{\an8}<i>please welcome Mr. Graydon Creed!</i>

32
00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.582
{\an8}[man] Humans were here first!

33
00:03:41.583 --> 00:03:44.374
They say Genosha was a tragedy.

34
00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:46.624
I say it was a consequence

35
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:50.249
of a world forced to live
in danger far too long.

36
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.291
If history has taught us anything.

37
00:03:52.292 --> 00:03:55.999
it's that mutants
can't be trusted with their powers.

38
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.541
And what does President Kelly do?
He gives them more.

39
00:03:59.542 --> 00:04:04.666
Using your tax dollars
to fund his X-Factor.

40
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:08.249
Not to protect you. but to protect them.

41
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.332
[woman] What about us?

42
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:11.291
Well. I say no longer.

43
00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:13.042
Yeah. not on your watch.

44
00:04:13.917 --> 00:04:16.582
For I have heard your call.

45
00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:19.041
and with your support. tonight.

46
00:04:19.042 --> 00:04:22.082
I officially announce my candidacy

47
00:04:22.083 --> 00:04:24.999
for President of the United States.

48
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.624
A leader for humanity.

49
00:04:27.625 --> 00:04:31.041
[crowd chanting] For humanity!
For humanity!

50
00:04:31.042 --> 00:04:34.249
For humanity! For humanity!

51
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.374
[gasps]

52
00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.958
[people screaming]

53
00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:42.000
[Creed screams]

54
00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:11.541
[Creed grunts] No. No!

55
00:05:11.542 --> 00:05:12.749
[guard] Hands in the air.

56
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.167
Stand down! Stand down!

57
00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:18.875
Sorry. But no.

58
00:05:29.583 --> 00:05:32.791
{\an8}<i>They call themselves
the Acolytes of Magneto.</i>

59
00:05:32.792 --> 00:05:38.167
{\an8}<i>An emerging cult of radical extremists
devoted to the late "Master of Magnetism"</i>

60
00:05:38.292 --> 00:05:40.624
{\an8}<i>and his vision for mutant supremacy.</i>

61
00:05:40.625 --> 00:05:44.124
{\an8}<i>Moments ago. the Acolyte leader
known as Exodus</i>

62
00:05:44.125 --> 00:05:47.707
{\an8}<i>released a statement
claiming responsibility for their attack.</i>

63
00:05:47.708 --> 00:05:51.666
{\an8}<i>Four thousand. six hundred
and twenty-one seconds.</i>

64
00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:54.916
That's how long it took
for Genosha to be reduced to ashes.

65
00:05:54.917 --> 00:05:58.916
And humanity's response?
Is to raise up men like this.

66
00:05:58.917 --> 00:06:01.916
Men who paint targets
on mutantkind's backs

67
00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:04.124
while we mourn our lost.

68
00:06:04.125 --> 00:06:08.832
<i>Magneto understood there is no appealing
to humanity's "better nature."</i>

69
00:06:08.833 --> 00:06:10.166
<i>for you have none.</i>

70
00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:13.041
<i>So instead. we make these demands.</i>

71
00:06:13.042 --> 00:06:17.082
<i>All mutants currently detained
by the race traitors known as X-Factor</i>

72
00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:18.582
<i>will be released.</i>

73
00:06:18.583 --> 00:06:21.749
<i>You will remand them to Acolyte custody.</i>

74
00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.791
<i>and you will stay out of our way.</i>

75
00:06:24.792 --> 00:06:26.208
<i>Fail to comply...</i>

76
00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:29.333
<i>Graydon Creed dies.</i>

77
00:06:32.417 --> 00:06:34.250
<i>I give you 24 hours.</i>

78
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.667
<i>Bonne journée.</i>

79
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.791
Graydon Creed deserves
about as much sympathy

80
00:06:40.792 --> 00:06:43.332
as a hungry crocodile
at a children's pettin' zoo.

81
00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:45.875
But I reckon this can't be simple for ya.

82
00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:49.124
In our family. sister.

83
00:06:49.125 --> 00:06:50.833
nothing ever is.

84
00:06:53.583 --> 00:06:56.957
Please tell me you're not going
to try to insert your people into this.

85
00:06:56.958 --> 00:07:00.249
I'm already working with the UN
to approve activating X-Factor.

86
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.624
You cannot expect me to sit by

87
00:07:02.625 --> 00:07:04.332
while Exodus and his followers

88
00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:06.957
twist Magnus's name to justify their war.

89
00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:09.791
So. you have located the Acolyte base.

90
00:07:09.792 --> 00:07:12.207
My X-Men are already on their way.

91
00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:13.916
Trust me. Dr. Cooper.

92
00:07:13.917 --> 00:07:17.000
Where they are going.
you would not wish to follow.

93
00:07:21.042 --> 00:07:23.249
Welcome to the Savage Land.

94
00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.166
One of Earth's deadliest habitats.

95
00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:29.124
A bio-evolutionary time capsule
quite literally frozen in time.

96
00:07:29.125 --> 00:07:30.666
Pre-historic wildlife?

97
00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:32.249
Ancient evil spirits?

98
00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.082
Don't forget the leftover experiments

99
00:07:34.083 --> 00:07:36.374
from when Mister Sinister
was king of the jungle.

100
00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:38.624
Great. More things that can kill us.

101
00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:41.374
There he goes. Our walking doomsday clock.

102
00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:44.291
Always with his eye
on the worst-case scenario.

103
00:07:44.292 --> 00:07:46.750
I may have read your file. Lucas.

104
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.917
[chuckles] So. what's your strategy?
Cause a scene?

105
00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:53.082
- May have read your file too.
- Just sayin'.

106
00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:55.457
Can't imagine there's anything
more dangerous here

107
00:07:55.458 --> 00:07:57.166
than the man we're rescuin'.

108
00:07:57.167 --> 00:07:59.457
Creed's actions may be detestable.

109
00:07:59.458 --> 00:08:03.583
But I like to believe
that no one is above salvation.

110
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.500
[thudding]

111
00:08:10.708 --> 00:08:11.874
[screams]

112
00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:14.332
I'm detecting a familiar energy field.

113
00:08:14.333 --> 00:08:17.292
Akin to a signature established
when Mister Sinister...

114
00:08:17.792 --> 00:08:19.291
Oh. no!

115
00:08:19.292 --> 00:08:21.249
You feel that?

116
00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.042
Some type of radiation.

117
00:08:27.458 --> 00:08:29.791
Oh. dear! Hold on everyone!

118
00:08:29.792 --> 00:08:32.541
[Polaris] Incoming
surface-to-air-missiles. on our six.

119
00:08:32.542 --> 00:08:34.083
[Beast] Taking evasive action!

120
00:08:34.958 --> 00:08:36.041
[Nightcrawler] We are hit!

121
00:08:36.042 --> 00:08:37.958
[Bishop] Losing pressure.
we're goin' down!

122
00:08:40.125 --> 00:08:41.749
Rogue. can you level us out?

123
00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.707
On it. Beast. Ahh!

124
00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:46.999
- [Nightcrawler] Rogue!
- My powers. They ain't workin'.

125
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.917
Our gifts have abandoned us.

126
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.375
- [screams]
- [Beast] Bishop!

127
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.958
Polaris. don't!

128
00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.749
Come on. come on.

129
00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:02.583
Closer. Closer.

130
00:09:08.542 --> 00:09:11.125
[both grunt]

131
00:09:16.875 --> 00:09:17.875
Well...

132
00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:20.333
at least we stuck the landing.

133
00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.750
[distant thumping]

134
00:09:30.125 --> 00:09:32.792
- [roars]
- [Bishop grunts]

135
00:09:40.458 --> 00:09:42.957
Startin' to see why they call it
the Savage Land.

136
00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:46.166
- Honestly. might be underselling it.
- [chuckles] Yeah.

137
00:09:46.167 --> 00:09:49.082
- [groans]
- Bishop? Are you all right?

138
00:09:49.083 --> 00:09:52.332
Before the jet got hit.
there was some sorta energy.

139
00:09:52.333 --> 00:09:54.791
I can feel my powers
building up inside me.

140
00:09:54.792 --> 00:09:56.374
but I can't release them.

141
00:09:56.375 --> 00:09:58.332
Sinister's old Inhibitor Tower.

142
00:09:58.333 --> 00:10:01.625
The Acolytes must have rebooted it
to suppress all of our mutant powers.

143
00:10:03.292 --> 00:10:04.666
How long can you contain it?

144
00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:07.207
Let's just say
I don't got a lotta time left.

145
00:10:07.208 --> 00:10:10.457
We need to find the others
and get Creed the hell outta here.

146
00:10:10.458 --> 00:10:11.750
[grunts]

147
00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:18.875
[metallic creaking]

148
00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:23.875
[grunts]

149
00:10:24.458 --> 00:10:27.041
- Greetings. comrades.
- Peter!

150
00:10:27.042 --> 00:10:29.041
[groans]

151
00:10:29.042 --> 00:10:31.999
Almost forgot what pain feels like. Ahh!

152
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.875
- Are you injured?
- I am now.

153
00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.208
Thank you for answering our prayers.

154
00:10:42.917 --> 00:10:44.041
Stand down.

155
00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:46.750
I know these mutants as friends.

156
00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.291
What brings you here?

157
00:10:49.292 --> 00:10:51.749
We're here to rescue your hostage

158
00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.625
so you and your Acolyte buddies
don't start World War Three.

159
00:10:55.292 --> 00:10:57.166
I cannot give him to you.

160
00:10:57.167 --> 00:10:58.707
[Nightcrawler] You misunderstand.

161
00:10:58.708 --> 00:11:00.583
Creed is my brother.

162
00:11:02.167 --> 00:11:03.791
Half-brother.

163
00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:06.792
He and I share a mother. Mystique.

164
00:11:07.625 --> 00:11:09.082
He is family.

165
00:11:09.083 --> 00:11:11.874
We do what we must for our kin.

166
00:11:11.875 --> 00:11:14.541
but I still cannot release Creed.

167
00:11:14.542 --> 00:11:18.166
We may not have powers here.
but we're not just gonna turn around--

168
00:11:18.167 --> 00:11:19.167
Rogue. please.

169
00:11:20.208 --> 00:11:23.166
Perhaps instead you will
allow us to tour your home

170
00:11:23.167 --> 00:11:24.874
and look upon your work.

171
00:11:24.875 --> 00:11:27.541
Should we come to understand your cause.

172
00:11:27.542 --> 00:11:29.916
imagine the message it would send.

173
00:11:29.917 --> 00:11:33.999
You would view our home with an open mind?

174
00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:38.125
So long as we can ensure
the prisoner is being treated fairly.

175
00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:40.457
Treat us with respect

176
00:11:40.458 --> 00:11:43.082
and we will return such.

177
00:11:43.083 --> 00:11:45.750
And perhaps your powers. too.

178
00:11:48.417 --> 00:11:50.125
We seek a simple life here.

179
00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.916
Food. water. and power.

180
00:11:53.917 --> 00:11:55.375
Simple concerns.

181
00:11:56.458 --> 00:12:00.082
Exodus found me in the darkest of places.

182
00:12:00.083 --> 00:12:03.166
He may have his eccentric qualities.

183
00:12:03.167 --> 00:12:06.166
but each day I have been here.

184
00:12:06.167 --> 00:12:09.332
another mutant finds safety.

185
00:12:09.333 --> 00:12:12.457
For that. he has given me a purpose

186
00:12:12.458 --> 00:12:14.750
and earned my trust.

187
00:12:15.375 --> 00:12:18.999
But your sister would never
want you to join the Acolytes.

188
00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.291
How can you know. Beast?

189
00:12:21.292 --> 00:12:25.208
How can any of us know
the desires of the dead?

190
00:12:32.583 --> 00:12:34.791
[Nightcrawler] A beautiful painting.

191
00:12:34.792 --> 00:12:35.792
Yours?

192
00:12:36.667 --> 00:12:37.958
To honor her.

193
00:12:46.125 --> 00:12:48.332
I'm sorry. Peter.

194
00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:51.166
The time for sentiment has passed. Rogue.

195
00:12:51.167 --> 00:12:54.332
Each of us must act
to ensure others like us

196
00:12:54.333 --> 00:12:57.292
will not lose their brothers and sisters.

197
00:12:58.375 --> 00:13:01.208
In this. we share the same goal.

198
00:13:03.542 --> 00:13:05.207
[door opens]

199
00:13:05.208 --> 00:13:07.500
Awaken. you have visitors.

200
00:13:08.583 --> 00:13:10.541
Greetings. brother.

201
00:13:10.542 --> 00:13:11.667
[Creed scoffs]

202
00:13:12.417 --> 00:13:16.750
A shame that even now
he cannot accept his kin.

203
00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.707
"He does not treat us as our sins deserve.

204
00:13:20.708 --> 00:13:23.332
or repay us according to our inequities.

205
00:13:23.333 --> 00:13:26.916
For as high as the heavens are
above the earth..."

206
00:13:26.917 --> 00:13:30.083
"So great is his love
for those who fear Him."

207
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.792
If you're going to kill me. kill me.

208
00:13:34.583 --> 00:13:36.583
Skip the sermons.

209
00:13:39.583 --> 00:13:43.917
How painful it must be
to be so hated by one's own family.

210
00:13:47.125 --> 00:13:48.208
Exodus.

211
00:13:51.708 --> 00:13:54.541
Colossus. I see you have brought friends

212
00:13:54.542 --> 00:13:56.083
to witness our crusade.

213
00:13:56.875 --> 00:13:58.666
Any mutant hand is welcome

214
00:13:58.667 --> 00:14:01.249
to help build
the better world we are creating.

215
00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.707
And in this world.

216
00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:06.416
you threaten to murder a man
without so much as a trial?

217
00:14:06.417 --> 00:14:09.249
You yourself
have born witness to his sins.

218
00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.332
And yet. he was exonerated
by humans at every turn.

219
00:14:13.333 --> 00:14:16.832
But we have not had
our day in court. have we?

220
00:14:16.833 --> 00:14:21.041
These were crimes
against our kind. Mutants.

221
00:14:21.042 --> 00:14:24.457
[scoffs] How brave and bold.

222
00:14:24.458 --> 00:14:28.082
You suggest a trial
here in the Savage Land?

223
00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:30.124
To prove what?

224
00:14:30.125 --> 00:14:32.582
Whether the soul of my brother

225
00:14:32.583 --> 00:14:35.042
is beyond all hope of redemption.

226
00:14:38.542 --> 00:14:41.374
- No. I ain't letting you--
- [in German] <i>Fräulein.</i>

227
00:14:41.375 --> 00:14:44.667
I have faith I can prove
our brother is worth redeeming.

228
00:14:45.667 --> 00:14:50.458
But does our dear Templar have faith
in his ability to prove otherwise?

229
00:14:55.667 --> 00:14:57.833
[Colossus] And if Exodus wins...

230
00:14:58.375 --> 00:15:00.000
What then?

231
00:15:01.458 --> 00:15:03.416
I will join your flock.

232
00:15:03.417 --> 00:15:05.957
- [Rogue] Kurt. don't.
- It's all right. sister.

233
00:15:05.958 --> 00:15:08.666
It will be a signal
to mutants across the world

234
00:15:08.667 --> 00:15:11.458
that even an X-Man can see the light.

235
00:15:12.208 --> 00:15:14.958
All this I offer. with one condition...

236
00:15:15.958 --> 00:15:18.708
Colossus will preside over the trial.

237
00:15:25.208 --> 00:15:26.791
[Polaris] They must've moved off.

238
00:15:26.792 --> 00:15:29.208
Nah. more like carted off.

239
00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.457
Place is a fortress.

240
00:15:33.458 --> 00:15:36.707
Gonna need a mighty big advantage
if we're gonna bust them out.

241
00:15:36.708 --> 00:15:40.124
Also. need you to not
implode on me before we get there.

242
00:15:40.125 --> 00:15:42.916
Then we better take out
that Inhibitor Tower first.

243
00:15:42.917 --> 00:15:45.124
Got any bright ideas?

244
00:15:45.125 --> 00:15:47.249
Bright? No.

245
00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.375
But fun?

246
00:15:49.417 --> 00:15:50.500
Hell. yeah.

247
00:15:57.958 --> 00:16:02.792
[Senyaka] The court of the Independent
Haven of our Lord Magnus is in session.

248
00:16:05.833 --> 00:16:08.083
Bring out the accused.

249
00:16:09.542 --> 00:16:12.500
I do not recognize this kangaroo court!

250
00:16:13.542 --> 00:16:17.250
No muties jury's ever
gonna let me walk. Ahh!

251
00:16:18.625 --> 00:16:20.957
[Colossus] Senyaka. behave yourself.

252
00:16:20.958 --> 00:16:23.875
This court will have order.

253
00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.875
Now. Exodus?

254
00:16:27.625 --> 00:16:29.375
Plead your case.

255
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.541
Thank you. honorable Colossus.

256
00:16:32.542 --> 00:16:36.124
Graydon Creed is a name
familiar to many in this room.

257
00:16:36.125 --> 00:16:38.291
He founded the Friends of Humanity.

258
00:16:38.292 --> 00:16:40.916
Created a virus that kills mutants.

259
00:16:40.917 --> 00:16:43.957
Tried to frame a mutant
for killing the President.

260
00:16:43.958 --> 00:16:46.957
The humans would not
make him pay for those crimes.

261
00:16:46.958 --> 00:16:49.500
Is it not just that we do?

262
00:16:50.333 --> 00:16:52.874
Creed is a serpent in our garden.

263
00:16:52.875 --> 00:16:57.332
whose wretched actions
are born from one original sin.

264
00:16:57.333 --> 00:16:59.667
a hatred of mutants.

265
00:17:00.708 --> 00:17:02.707
[audience clamoring]

266
00:17:02.708 --> 00:17:04.250
Freaking bigot!

267
00:17:04.667 --> 00:17:06.541
The prosecution rests.

268
00:17:06.542 --> 00:17:08.332
Thank you. Exodus.

269
00:17:08.333 --> 00:17:11.250
Nightcrawler. for the defense.

270
00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:17.457
So. why do you hate mutants?

271
00:17:17.458 --> 00:17:20.000
[scoffs] How long we got?

272
00:17:20.792 --> 00:17:23.458
Let us err on the side of brevity.

273
00:17:24.583 --> 00:17:27.083
Because you were born.

274
00:17:27.875 --> 00:17:30.250
What are we even doing this for?

275
00:17:30.833 --> 00:17:31.957
Ah.

276
00:17:31.958 --> 00:17:34.082
<i>Und</i> how were you born. brother?

277
00:17:34.083 --> 00:17:36.207
Were you born with powers?

278
00:17:36.208 --> 00:17:38.375
[chuckles] Heck. no.

279
00:17:39.208 --> 00:17:42.457
Strange. born with no powers.

280
00:17:42.458 --> 00:17:45.750
considering we both were born
of a mutant mother Mystique.

281
00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:50.416
Last I checked.
she chucked you off a waterfall.

282
00:17:50.417 --> 00:17:51.875
[audience gasping]

283
00:17:53.125 --> 00:17:55.166
What about that scar?

284
00:17:55.167 --> 00:17:56.542
Were you born with that?

285
00:17:57.583 --> 00:18:00.042
Ah. it seems to be a claw mark.

286
00:18:00.208 --> 00:18:01.707
Your father.

287
00:18:01.708 --> 00:18:04.208
His name is Sabretooth.

288
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.874
That man is not my father!

289
00:18:07.875 --> 00:18:10.916
The defendant will take his seat

290
00:18:10.917 --> 00:18:13.374
and answer the question.

291
00:18:13.375 --> 00:18:15.333
[Creed] You got no idea.

292
00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:20.583
Think you're the only guy
who's had it hard. hmm?

293
00:18:21.458 --> 00:18:24.500
Our mother booted me as a baby.

294
00:18:24.625 --> 00:18:25.625
but Sabretooth.

295
00:18:26.458 --> 00:18:27.958
he wanted a cub.

296
00:18:29.167 --> 00:18:32.500
And when I couldn't live up to his name...

297
00:18:33.042 --> 00:18:34.583
He would punish you?

298
00:18:35.333 --> 00:18:38.542
Calls himself Sabretooth.
what do you think?

299
00:18:40.042 --> 00:18:42.417
Every night. I reminded myself.

300
00:18:43.167 --> 00:18:44.875
make it to 13.

301
00:18:45.625 --> 00:18:47.500
I'd get powers like he did.

302
00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.208
Then I could hunt like him.

303
00:18:50.875 --> 00:18:52.292
Hell. even better.

304
00:18:53.375 --> 00:18:55.416
But you were human.

305
00:18:55.417 --> 00:18:58.124
And so he abandoned you.

306
00:18:58.125 --> 00:19:00.208
just like our mother did.

307
00:19:03.042 --> 00:19:06.542
Graydon. you do not hate mutants.

308
00:19:07.375 --> 00:19:10.041
You hate the two who hurt you.

309
00:19:10.042 --> 00:19:11.832
who failed you.

310
00:19:11.833 --> 00:19:14.875
who made you feel like
being human wasn't good enough.

311
00:19:15.917 --> 00:19:19.749
<i>Und</i> even now. with your life on the line.

312
00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.999
you let them control you.

313
00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.666
let them make you risk your life

314
00:19:24.667 --> 00:19:27.999
just so you can continue hating them.

315
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.792
When all you need to do
is forgive yourself

316
00:19:32.833 --> 00:19:36.958
for thinking you weren't strong enough.

317
00:19:41.333 --> 00:19:43.875
[sighing] Oh. enough of this.

318
00:19:46.625 --> 00:19:47.791
Colossus.

319
00:19:47.792 --> 00:19:49.583
speak the verdict.

320
00:19:50.292 --> 00:19:51.875
Peter. please!

321
00:19:52.417 --> 00:19:54.083
I know you see it.

322
00:19:54.625 --> 00:19:58.083
He is just a man. haunted.

323
00:19:59.625 --> 00:20:01.958
Just like us.

324
00:20:04.625 --> 00:20:07.542
I find the defendant...

325
00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.250
Heretic!

326
00:20:12.958 --> 00:20:14.750
- Peter!
- Let him go. Exodus!

327
00:20:15.583 --> 00:20:16.832
Put him down!

328
00:20:16.833 --> 00:20:19.582
This is how you honor your sister?

329
00:20:19.583 --> 00:20:21.041
[Colossus groans]

330
00:20:21.042 --> 00:20:24.041
[Exodus] Fine.
Let me reunite you with her

331
00:20:24.042 --> 00:20:27.374
so you may see
the disappointment on her face.

332
00:20:27.375 --> 00:20:31.292
[screams]

333
00:20:33.167 --> 00:20:34.167
Hmm?

334
00:20:37.125 --> 00:20:39.082
Target the Inhibitor Tower.

335
00:20:39.083 --> 00:20:41.167
Time to turn the power on!

336
00:20:44.875 --> 00:20:46.000
Ha-ha!

337
00:20:48.792 --> 00:20:50.458
No! No. no.

338
00:20:52.125 --> 00:20:53.583
[grunts]

339
00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.792
- [Bishop screams]
- [Polaris grunts]

340
00:21:05.542 --> 00:21:07.166
No more holdin' it in.

341
00:21:07.167 --> 00:21:09.124
Let's end this with a bang!

342
00:21:09.125 --> 00:21:11.167
[all screaming]

343
00:21:26.625 --> 00:21:28.041
[chuckles softly]

344
00:21:28.042 --> 00:21:30.667
[pants] Ahh!

345
00:21:33.583 --> 00:21:36.708
Your death shall salvage the day.

346
00:21:39.625 --> 00:21:42.374
Pray you wield your sword
better than your tongue.

347
00:21:42.375 --> 00:21:43.500
En garde!

348
00:22:05.042 --> 00:22:06.958
[groans] Huh?

349
00:22:19.125 --> 00:22:21.792
You truly are a demon.

350
00:22:27.542 --> 00:22:28.542
[gasps]

351
00:22:33.917 --> 00:22:36.041
You are as you were born. Exodus.

352
00:22:36.042 --> 00:22:39.707
A vain soul clamoring
for his 15 minutes of faith.

353
00:22:39.708 --> 00:22:41.291
Yield!

354
00:22:41.292 --> 00:22:44.542
[scoffs] My faith
will keep me protected from--

355
00:22:53.375 --> 00:22:55.416
Get me out of this freak show.

356
00:22:55.417 --> 00:22:56.999
or I will blow your brains out.

357
00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:59.624
- Brother. what have you done?
- What I have always done.

358
00:22:59.625 --> 00:23:00.791
Survived.

359
00:23:00.792 --> 00:23:02.750
- Polaris!
- On it.

360
00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.207
"You cannot conceive. nor can I.

361
00:23:19.208 --> 00:23:22.333
the appalling strangeness
of the mercy of God."

362
00:23:25.208 --> 00:23:28.582
But who. more than you. deserves to die

363
00:23:28.583 --> 00:23:30.416
for the horrors you have unleashed?

364
00:23:30.417 --> 00:23:32.207
[groans]

365
00:23:32.208 --> 00:23:34.499
For would it really be mercy

366
00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:37.916
to spare the monster
who would let mutants suffer?

367
00:23:37.917 --> 00:23:41.750
Or is mercy found
in ending you and sparing us instead?

368
00:23:43.792 --> 00:23:48.458
Alas. this is what higher powers are for.

369
00:23:49.042 --> 00:23:53.000
But allow me to grant you this. brother...

370
00:23:54.083 --> 00:23:56.041
You may not be a mutant.

371
00:23:56.042 --> 00:24:00.625
but you are very much your parents' son.

372
00:24:02.708 --> 00:24:06.208
[coughs]

373
00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:18.207
<i>So X-Factor found Creed alone.</i>

374
00:24:18.208 --> 00:24:20.374
wandering in the snow.

375
00:24:20.375 --> 00:24:23.957
Alone. but alive. As promised.

376
00:24:23.958 --> 00:24:27.542
You're playing a very
dangerous game. Charles.

377
00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:31.666
Cross the line and. our history or not.

378
00:24:31.667 --> 00:24:33.999
I'll take away your corporation

379
00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:35.667
and your school.

380
00:24:42.917 --> 00:24:45.333
[Nightcrawler] Welcome home.
[in German] <i>mein Freund.</i>

381
00:24:46.875 --> 00:24:49.250
I sense you have a question. comrade.

382
00:24:51.458 --> 00:24:52.750
I do.

383
00:24:53.167 --> 00:24:54.916
My verdict?

384
00:24:54.917 --> 00:24:56.875
Did I make my case?

385
00:24:57.750 --> 00:25:00.792
No. you did not convince me.

386
00:25:01.875 --> 00:25:03.457
But...

387
00:25:03.458 --> 00:25:06.500
you would have convinced Illyana.

388
00:25:42.458 --> 00:25:43.792
[Cable and Jubilee gasp]

389
00:25:47.417 --> 00:25:48.749
How?

390
00:25:48.750 --> 00:25:50.000
How could this be?

391
00:25:50.875 --> 00:25:53.125
Um. guys...

392
00:25:57.375 --> 00:25:59.375
[closing theme music playing]
